-- title:
--   Transport of a semilinear chart datum between two Drinfeld charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \neq 2$, a discrete valuation domain $A$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $\varpi$, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$, and an element $t \in \mathfrak m_A$. Let $W_0$ and $W$ be discrete valuation domains, complete for their maximal ideals, with ring maps $\sigma_0 : A \to W_0$ and $\sigma : A \to W$ such that $\mathfrak m_{W_0} = (\sigma_0\varpi)$ and $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$. Let $f_0,u_0,v_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_0,v_0$ units and $f_0 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and likewise $f,u,v$ over $W$; put $S_0 = W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_0 t)v_0 - f_0u_0)$ and $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma t)v - fu)$, both assumed local, with $S$ moreover Hausdorff for $\mathfrak m_S$, and write $J_0, J$ for the ideals generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$. Given a ring isomorphism $\beta : S_0 \simeq S$, a commutative ring $D$ with maps $\psi_0 : D \to S_0$, $\psi : D \to S$, a ring endomorphism $\tau$ of $D$, a ring automorphism $\sigma_A$ of $A$, an element $x \in A$, a $2\times2$ matrix $N$ of natural numbers, an automorphism $\theta_0$ of $S_0$, an automorphism $\sigma_{W_0}$ of $W_0$, an element $c_0 \in W_0$ and a $2\times2$ matrix $M_0$ over $W_0$, assume: $\beta$ carries the constant $\sigma_0 a$ to the constant $\sigma a$ for all $a \in A$; every $w \in W_0$ (resp. $w \in W$) is congruent to some $\sigma_0 a$ (resp. $\sigma a$) in the sense that the image of $C(w - \sigma_0 a)$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{S_0}$ (resp. $\mathfrak m_S$); $\beta \circ \psi_0 = \psi$; the image of $\psi_0$ is dense, i.e. each $s \in S_0$ and $n$ admit $d \in D$ with $s - \psi_0 d \in \mathfrak m_{S_0}^n$; for each $g \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z/q)$ there are an integral matrix $G$ reducing to $g$ mod $q$, an endomorphism $\tau_g$ of $D$, automorphisms $\theta_{0,g}$ of $S_0$ and $\theta_g$ of $S$ compatible with $\tau_g$ through $\psi_0$ and $\psi$, fixing all constants from $W_0$ resp. $W$, whose linear parts are given modulo $J_0^2$ resp. $J^2$ by matrices $M_{0,g}$, $M_g$ congruent to $G$ modulo the maximal ideals; and finally that $\theta_0$ realises $\tau$ on the first chart, namely $\theta_0\psi_0 = \psi_0\tau$, $\sigma_{W_0}\sigma_0 = \sigma_0\sigma_A$, $\sigma_{W_0} \equiv \mathrm{id} \bmod \mathfrak m_{W_0}$, $\theta_0(C w) = C(\sigma_{W_0}w)$, $\theta_0(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_0(i,j)X_i \bmod J_0^2$, $c_0 \equiv \sigma_0 x$ and $M_0(i,j) \equiv c_0 N(i,j)$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an automorphism $\sigma_W$ of $W$, an element $c \in W$ and a $2\times2$ matrix $M$ over $W$ satisfying the seven corresponding conditions on the second chart: $\theta\psi = \psi\tau$, $\sigma_W\sigma = \sigma\sigma_A$, $\sigma_W \equiv \mathrm{id} \bmod \mathfrak m_W$, $\theta(C w) = C(\sigma_W w)$, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M(i,j)X_i \bmod J^2$, $c \equiv \sigma x$ and $M(i,j) \equiv c\,N(i,j)$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   This is the purely algebraic form of the chart-transport step in the theory of Drinfeld level structures (Katz–Mazur 13.7–13.8): a semilinear automorphism of one Drinfeld chart, with prescribed residual linear part $c N$, is carried across an isomorphism of the two chart rings to a semilinear automorphism of the other chart with the same shape of linear part. It is used in the determination of the action of inertia on the Drinfeld charts of modular curves of full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense.lean

import Mathlib
